{"name":"Fall River","hex":"#f59344","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Fall River","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city in Bristol County, Massachusetts, United States.","A river in South Dakota, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Fall_River"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fall River, Nova Scotia","blocks":[{"text":"Fall River is a suburban community located in Nova Scotia, Canada within the Halifax Regional Municipality. It is located north-northeast of the Bedford Basin, northeast of Bedford and Lower Sackville and north of Waverley."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fall_River%2C_Nova_Scotia"},{"title":"Fall River, Massachusetts","blocks":[{"text":"Fall River is a city in Bristol County, Massachusetts, United States. Fall River's population was 94,000 at the 2020 United States census, making it the tenth-largest city in the state, and the second-largest municipality in the county behind New Bedford. It abuts the Rhode Island state line with Tiverton, Rhode Island, to its south."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Bank_Street_Fall_River.jpg/330px-Bank_Street_Fall_River.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fall_River%2C_Massachusetts"},{"title":"Autumn","blocks":[{"text":"Autumn, also known as fall in North American English, is one of the four temperate seasons on Earth. Outside the tropics, autumn marks the transition from summer to winter, beginning in September or March. Autumn is the season when the duration of daytime becomes noticeably shorter and the temperature cools considerably. Day length decreases and night length increases as the season progresses until the winter solstice in December and June. One of its main features in temperate climates is the striking change in colour of the leaves of deciduous trees as they prepare to shed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/D%C3%BClmen%2C_Wildpark_--_2014_--_3808_color_balanced.jpg/330px-D%C3%BClmen%2C_Wildpark_--_2014_--_3808_color_balanced.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autumn"},{"title":"River","blocks":[{"text":"A river is a natural stream of fresh water that flows on land or inside caves towards another body of water at a lower elevation, such as an ocean, lake, or another river. A river may run dry before reaching the end of its course if it runs out of water, or only flow during certain seasons. Rivers are regulated by the water cycle, the processes by which water moves around the Earth. Water first enters rivers through precipitation, whether from rainfall, the runoff of water down a slope, the melting of glaciers or snow, or seepage from aquifers beneath the surface of the Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg/330px-Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/NS_Trunk_2_FallRiver.jpg/500px-NS_Trunk_2_FallRiver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/NS_Trunk_2_FallRiver.jpg/1280px-NS_Trunk_2_FallRiver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/NS_Trunk_2_FallRiver.jpg/500px-NS_Trunk_2_FallRiver.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nova Scotia Trunk 2 forms one of the main thoroughfares in Fall River. Portions of Trunk 2, Fall River Road and Blue Hill Road were originally part of the Great Road between Halifax and Truro.[3]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANS_Trunk_2_FallRiver.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/2021_St._Anne%27s_Church%2C_Fall_River.jpg/500px-2021_St._Anne%27s_Church%2C_Fall_River.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/2021_St._Anne%27s_Church%2C_Fall_River.jpg/1280px-2021_St._Anne%27s_Church%2C_Fall_River.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/2021_St._Anne%27s_Church%2C_Fall_River.jpg/500px-2021_St._Anne%27s_Church%2C_Fall_River.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2021_St._Anne's_Church%2C_Fall_River.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Battleship_Cove_FR.jpg/500px-Battleship_Cove_FR.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Battleship_Cove_FR.jpg/500px-Battleship_Cove_FR.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABattleship_Cove_FR.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Lizzie_Borden_House_%28Bed_Breakfast%29_%283535957840%29.jpg/500px-Lizzie_Borden_House_%28Bed_Breakfast%29_%283535957840%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Lizzie_Borden_House_%28Bed_Breakfast%29_%283535957840%29.jpg/1280px-Lizzie_Borden_House_%28Bed_Breakfast%29_%283535957840%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Lizzie_Borden_House_%28Bed_Breakfast%29_%283535957840%29.jpg/5